    "result_text": "All 21 tests pass, including the new Cp12 normalization tests and the household tests (Cp10/Cp11) that now compare normalized addresses.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented address normalization on owner creation in `OwnerRestControllerV1`:\n\n- **`normalizeAddress(...)`** \u2014 trims and collapses internal whitespace to single spaces, upper-cases, and expands street-type abbreviations token-by-token via a `ADDRESS_ABBREVIATIONS` map (`ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`). A `null` address passes through untouched so the required-field check can still report it as missing; a whitespace-only address normalizes to `\"\"`.\n- **Wired into `addOwner`** as the first step, before `validateRequiredFields`. This writes the normalized value back onto the request DTO, so:\n  - It's **stored and returned** in normalized form (`\"  12  main  st \"` \u2192 `\"12 MAIN STREET\"`).\n  - The **required-field check rejects addresses blank after normalization** (`\"   \"` \u2192 `\"\"` \u2192 400).\n  - **Household duplicate detection** and the **household id** both derive from `owner.getAddress()`, which is now the normalized value, so they compare the normalized form (existing owners were created through the same path, so both sides are consistently normalized).\n\nI only touched the create path (`addOwner`), matching the spec's \"whenever an owner is created\"; `updateOwner` was intentionally left unchanged.",
